The massive oceanic pressures collapsed upon Marina, shattering her aquatic heart and scattering her restless spirit throughout the sea’s expanse. Pelagos believed he had preserved his still dominion forever. He was entirely wrong.

Today, when the oceans swell and crash, mortals watch new waves rise. The roaring tides are Marina’s scattered essence—a wild, brilliant rebellion of shifting water, forever banishing eternal stagnation from the sea.

